Infrared evidence relates bands, mixtures and observed amount (@cm-residue-infrared: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/sources/Analytical-Chemistry-Harvey.lingua#r_0XMY75E3FRXRGR3BK28V3JAC0T", #source "../sources/Nonvolatile-Residue-Collection-and-Analysis-NASA.lingua#r_2YMCRSWR07NCHECM0X4D8FJ6HJ", #clean-manufacturing "Chromatography-and-mass-spectra-supply-complementary-evidence.lingua#r_2QKJC6Z59PH7NK3G5Y0N9TS23K") { r_3NDNVBAZBYZS0TM9J2XPVK51J9
**Read:** [Analytical Chemistry 2.1 — David Harvey](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/sources/Analytical-Chemistry-Harvey.lingua#r_0XMY75E3FRXRGR3BK28V3JAC0T), chapter 10; [Nonvolatile residue collection and analysis — Gordon, Rutherford and Aranda](../sources/Nonvolatile-Residue-Collection-and-Analysis-NASA.lingua#r_2YMCRSWR07NCHECM0X4D8FJ6HJ), infrared discussion. Reuse [Use a spectrum as chemical evidence with an observation model](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/measurement/Spectroscopic-evidence-and-calibration.lingua#r_5KF8FB97G6AMW8SNB4Y21E2ZHZ) for calibration and spectral interpretation.

Infrared features can support assignments of molecular vibrations and functional groups. Overlapping bands, the specimen's environment and mixtures affect the interpretation. A familiar band can narrow the possibilities without uniquely identifying every component.

For a transmission experiment under a valid linear absorbance model, A(ν) = ℓΣ ε_i(ν)c_i. The path length and coefficients must match the measurement. A deposited film or an attenuated-total-reflection observation has a different geometry; directly inserting an arbitrary bulk path length can give a misleading amount.

**Example:** Let two normalized observations have response rows (1, 0.2) and (0.1, 1). Component amounts (2, 1) give observations (2.2, 1.2). These distinguish the two components in the exact model. If their response columns become identical, the same observations determine only a combination of amounts. More fitted digits do not restore the missing distinction.

**Work:** Recover the two amounts and perturb the responses and observations. Compare a known-reference mixture with an unknown residue having additional components. State what a spectrum supports about identity, what calibration is needed for quantity, and which complementary separation or elemental observation would challenge the interpretation.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
